caverns dozens of meters underground, with no light source except
the occasional lantern if you're lucky.  And yet your eyes have
adjusted to the point where even without a light source you can
still see clearly several meters in all directions.  Then you climb
what you think is a normal set of stairs, and suddenly you see the
sun, radiating more light than you've seen in all the dungeons up
to this point.  So who's blind?  Well, you are.


